\tag{fdip}
\title{Central twists and exact coupled sums}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{A central twist changes a cyclic holonomy without
changing elementary plaquettes. It can therefore force
a pure-gauge loop average to vanish. A matter determinant
is gauge invariant, but need not preserve this extra
symmetry. An exact finite sign model exhibits both the
changed loop mean and a nonzero dressed pair.}

